From c9cb74725c887d91a3107a02cccfec737eb897b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:31:39 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 106/152] ASoC: samsung: Add Exynos9810 A-Box firmware-less
 driver

Samsung's A-Box driver loads the Calliope DSP firmware and lets it
program the RDMA/WDMA engines. Program them from Linux instead, with the
register layout recovered from the firmware's own accessors
(calliope_sram.bin 0x209c-0x2330 for RDMA at 0x17c51000,
calliope_dram.bin 0x80002b6a-0x80002d18 for WDMA at 0x17c52000):

  CTRL0: [0] enable, [4] buffer type, [5] update, [12:8] format,
         [13] mono expand, [18:16] function, [22:19] burst length
  0x08 BUF_STR, 0x0c BUF_END, 0x10 BUF_OFFSET (period), 0x14 STR_POINT,
  0x18 VOL_FACTOR, 0x1c VOL_CHANGE, 0x20 SBANK limit, 0x30 status

The routing, SPUS/SPUM and UAIF register fields are the ones of the
downstream regmap (abox.c, abox_if.c). Routes are fixed: RDMA0 -> SIFS1
-> UAIF0, RDMA1 -> SIFS2 -> UAIF1, UAIFn -> NSRCn -> WDMAn+1, ASRC off.
The DMA interrupts only reach the A-Box GIC, so periods are emulated with
an hrtimer and the position comes from the DMA status register.

Without a CMU_AUD clock driver the node can ask the driver to set
PLL_AUD to 1179.648 MHz, AUDIF to 24.576 MHz and the UAIF dividers itself
(samsung,cmu-bringup), following the downstream CMUCAL sequences.

Bring-up helpers: a 'regs' sysfs dump and a 'tone' sysfs self test that
plays a square wave through RDMA0/1 without ALSA userspace.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
